      "bbox": null,
      "coordinate_space": null,
      "image_path": null,
      "caption_source": null,
      "caption_locator": null,
      "content": "CUDA Unified Memory supports all atomic operations available to host and device threads,\nenabling all threads to cooperate by concurrently accessing the same shared memory location.\nThe CUDA C++ standard library\nprovides many heterogeneous synchronization primitives tuned for concurrent use between host and device threads,\nincluding cuda::atomic, cuda::atomic_ref, cuda::barrier, cuda::semaphore, among many others.",
      "truncated": false,
      "metadata": {
        "collection": "official",
        "document_id": "cuda-unified-memory-programming",
        "url": "https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/archive/13.0.1/cuda-c-programming-guide/index.html#unified-memory-programming",
        "commit": null,
        "release": "13.0.1",
        "sha256": "360b2b02922954808049d9df6ff54db82db327e5aacfe9a44f80f5a4f2556946",
